# Redis Reliability

- Reuse the existing Compose Redis 7 instance. Do not add a second Redis or database.
- Laravel and Node must share the exact key namespace (`WS_TICKET_REDIS_PREFIX`, default `battle-arena:ws-ticket:`), SHA-256 hex digest, JSON metadata shape, and TTL (~30s). Bypass Laravel's global `REDIS_PREFIX` for ticket keys (dedicated/raw client) so Node does not double-prefix.
- Ticket consumption is atomic `GETDEL` only — never GET-then-DEL. No silent in-memory ticket cache fallback.
- Readiness (`GET /health/ready`) must fail when Redis cannot redeem tickets. Liveness may still pass.
- Bound reconnect/backoff. If Redis disconnects mid-flight, new handshakes fail closed.
- Keep command clients separate from any future Pub/Sub subscriber client. Redis Pub/Sub is at-most-once signaling only — never authoritative battle state.
- Do not persist account or battle data on the Node filesystem.

```ts
// ✅ Redis key
`${prefix}${sha256Hex(ticket)}` // e.g. battle-arena:ws-ticket:<64-hex>
```
